statement=('For every fixed integer r>=1, let p=2^-r and g_L be the product of m=4^L disjoint signs 1-2 A_L on width-L conjunctions, and F_L=2 A_r(1+g_L)/2-1. In the one-actual-gate representation with lambda=1, M=1 and any full physical coordinate order, the normalized root component is exactly zero. With I_g=2L2^L, its natural rank expectation obeys R(F_L)/I(F_L)>=[(8L-23)/12-r] I_g/(I_g+2r) whenever the right side is positive. The actual complete all-partition nonempty run-cost expectation obeys C(F_L)>=(6/(5 ln 2))[R(F_L)-I(F_L)], so its ratio to influence diverges uniformly over full orders, while H(F_L)/I(F_L)<=4+(1+r)/(p I_g). Moreover balanced tensor-seed activations with the same exactly zero root component preserve any Boolean seed h ratio H(h)/I(h) in the tensor limit; the optimal entropy/influence constant of the zero-root class equals that of unrestricted FEI. This does not assert a bound or obstruction for multiple ordered covers, other gate representations, or all successful repeat-visit queue runs.')
